  "answer": "LIST v FROM PhysicalProperty has PhysicalPropertyMassjup m AND ALSO has PhysicalPropertyRadjup r AND ALSO ((m * 317.83) / (r * 11.209)) AS mrr AND ALSO (((m * 317.83) * 797.14256) / ((r * 11.209) * 6.371)) AS a AND ALSO ((500 + a / 500) / 2) AS g1 AND ALSO ((g1 + a / g1) / 2) AS g2 AND ALSO ((g2 + a / g2) / 2) AS g3 AND ALSO ((g3 + a / g3) / 2) AS g4 AND ALSO ((g4 + a / g4) / 2) AS g5 AND ALSO ((g5 + a / g5) / 2) AS g6 AND ALSO round(g6) AS v WHERE m <> 0 AND r <> 0 ORDERED WITH mrr DESCENDING THE FIRST 1",
  "note": "ConQuer has no sqrt, so the escape velocity's square root is done by six Newton-Raphson steps from a constant guess of 500 km/s (converged well before the sixth). The radicand is 2*G*M/R expressed in km^2/s^2 with G = 6.674e-11, Earth mass 5.972e24 kg and Earth radius 6.371e6 m folded into the literal 797.14256. Result 586 km/s for the highest-MRR planet (18.86 MJ, 0.195 RJ)."
